<title>FRANCE: Breakdown of French grain export bids.</title>
<headline>Breakdown of French grain export bids.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grain traders gave the following cumulative breakdown of free market grain export bids placed through France at the European Union's weekly grain tender.</p>
<p>Bids for export refunds are in Ecus per tonne.</p>
<p>	    Refund	     Cumulative tonnage</p>
<p> WHEAT    5.87			  29,000</p>
<p>	    6.34 or less		87,000</p>
<p>	    6.50 or less	     240,000</p>
<p>	    7.50 or less	     409,000</p>
<p>	    7.94 or less	     423,000</p>
<p>	   13.50 or less	     622,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p>	   29.95			  11,000</p>
<p>	   31.00 or less		31,000</p>
<p>	   32.00 or less		66,000</p>
<p>	   34.00 or less	     161,000</p>
<p>	   35.00 or less	     253,000</p>
<p>	   35.94 or less	     278,000</p>
<p>RYE</p>
<p>	   29.75			   4,000</p>
<p>	   31.00 or less		 9,000</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
<p>/vmp/dom</p>
</text>
